course: dictionary
lesson: 750
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. You work out which meaning fits by reading the words around it. «The battery in my torch is flat.» Torch and flat are the clues: here a battery is a small object that stores electricity.
explain: The same word can mean something very different. «The doctor gave her a battery of tests.» You cannot hold a set of tests in your hand, so battery must mean a whole group of similar things. Ask: what would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
explain: Some words are about safety. «A swallowed button battery can burn through the throat in about two hours, so it is always an emergency.» The word emergency tells you it is urgent, so you must get help at once. Never open, burn or crush a battery.
fact: A battery is a small object that stores electricity and gives it to torches, toys, phones and remote controls.
fact: A battery can also mean a row or group of similar things, such as «a battery of tests».
fact: A battery stores energy in chemicals and pushes electricity round a circuit.
fact: A «flat battery» means an empty battery, with no electricity left to give.
fact: A swallowed button battery is an emergency: get help at once.
exercise: «The battery in my torch is flat.» What does battery mean here? | A set of large guns | A row or group of similar things | The crime of hitting someone | *A small object that stores electricity
exercise: «The doctor gave her a battery of tests.» What does battery mean here? | *A row or group of similar things | A small object that stores electricity | The crime of hitting someone | A set of large guns
exercise: «A swallowed button battery can burn through the throat in about two hours, so it is always an emergency.» Which word shows that the situation is urgent? | swallowed | *emergency | throat | hours
test: «Electricity only flows when it has a complete loop to go round; that loop is called a circuit.» What is a circuit? | A small object that stores electricity | A row of similar things | *A complete loop for electricity to flow round | A set of large guns
test: Jayden asks, «Can I put a battery in the fire to get rid of it?» What is the answer? | Yes, fire is the best way to get rid of it | Yes, if the battery is flat | *No, never burn a battery | No, but you can crush it instead
exam: Which phrase means a battery with no electricity left? | charge the battery | battery-powered | rechargeable battery | *flat battery
